{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"corking-phonolite-drafthorse","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\n`make venv` fails on this macOS/arm64 host for any NEW worktree:\n\n```\nERROR: selected uv is version 0.13.6, but this repository requires 0.12.7.\n       selected uv: /Users/joeoakhart/.local/share/uv-pins/0.12.7/uv\n       required by: pyproject.toml [tool.uv].required-version\n```\n\nThe error names the contradiction exactly: the binary living at the path `…/uv-pins/**0.12.7**/uv` reported `uv 0.13.6 (329bf9448 2026-10-26 aarch64-apple-darwin)`. The pin directory is a version-named path, and the binary inside it had been replaced in place with a NEWER build — dated the same day the failure appeared, and with the directory mtime inside the active session window.\n\n`uvx` in the same directory was untouched and still reported `0.12.7 (61291a8ca 2026-08-27)`. So exactly one of the two binaries was swapped, which is the signature of an in-place self-update of `uv` alone (`uv self update` rewrites the running binary at its own path) rather than of a re-provisioned pin directory.\n\n## Impact\nThis breaks worktree creation, which is the documented entry point for ALL work in this repo (`make worktree name=<branch>`, and the `make venv` + `make install` bootstrap in `docs/local-dev-env.md`). It fails closed and the message is accurate, so it is not silent — but it is also not self-describing: the path says `0.12.7` while the binary says `0.13.6`, which reads as a repo misconfiguration rather than a mutated host file.\n\nExisting worktrees are unaffected — their `.venv` directories already exist, so nothing re-resolves `uv`. The failure therefore appears only when a new worktree is provisioned, which is precisely when an agent is starting new work.\n\nA version-named directory whose contents can be silently rewritten is not a pin. It is a naming convention with no enforcement.\n\n## Verified workaround (applied on this host, not committed)\nRestore the matching release binary at the pinned path:\n\n```sh\ncd ~/.local/share/uv-pins/0.12.7\ncp uv uv.0.13.6.bak\ncurl -sL -o /tmp/uv.tgz \\\n  https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.12.7/uv-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz\ntar xzf /tmp/uv.tgz -C /tmp && cp /tmp/uv-aarch64-apple-darwin/uv ./uv && chmod +x ./uv\n```\n\n`uv --version` then reports `0.12.7 (61291a8ca 2026-08-27)` and `make venv` succeeds (`Using CPython 3.12.14`, venv created). The displaced 0.13.6 binary is kept alongside as `uv.0.13.6.bak`.\n\n## Proposed fix (needs a decision)\nThe workaround repairs one host. Options for preventing recurrence, in rough order of preference:\n\n1. **Verify the pin, not just its path.** Have the `make venv` preflight compare `uv --version` against `[tool.uv] required-version` BEFORE selecting the binary, and on mismatch fetch the required release into the pin directory automatically. Self-healing, portable, no CI-provider coupling.\n2. **Make the pin directory immutable** (read-only mode bits on the binary), so an in-place self-update fails loudly at the moment it happens rather than at the next worktree creation.\n3. **Content-address the pin** — name the directory by the release's checksum, so a replaced binary no longer resolves and the mismatch cannot masquerade as the pinned version.\n4. **Document only**, in `docs/local-dev-env.md`: record the failure signature and the restore recipe. Cheapest, but leaves the next agent to rediscover it.\n\nOption 1 is recommended but NOT yet decided: it needs confirmation that fetching a release binary during bootstrap is acceptable in this project's supply-chain posture (`docs/local-dev-env.md`, and the dependency-update rules in `CONTRIBUTING.md` §5).\n\nUnverified: what actually ran the update. No shell history or installer log was inspected, so `uv self update` is inferred from the single-binary swap and the in-place rewrite, not observed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] On a host whose pin directory holds a mismatched binary, `make venv` either repairs the pin or fails with a message that names the mutation (\"the binary at <pinned path> reports <X>, not the <Y> its path claims\") rather than only the version mismatch.\n- [ ] A newly provisioned worktree (`make worktree name=<x>`) completes `make venv` and `make install` with no manual intervention on such a host.\n- [ ] The chosen mechanism introduces no CI-provider-specific trigger: it runs from the documented local bootstrap, not only from a GitHub Actions step.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` records the failure signature and the operator restore recipe.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","id":"0461-3c72-9e38-4ce5","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make venv fails for new worktrees: the uv binary inside the 0.12.7 pin directory was replaced with 0.13.6"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793101163345989141,"uuid":"ea8ea416-6855-4031-badb-8e22e75f7db7"}